  "id": "DrugBank_DB00620 - MONDO_5480",
  "verbalization": "Tiamcinolone, a corticosteroid, is implicated in the development of contact dermatitis through a multi-step pathway involving its use as an indication for lichen disease, neurodermatitis, and occupational dermatitis. These conditions are all associated with inflammation and skin irritation, which are key drivers of contact dermatitis. The evidence suggests that Triamcinolone may contribute to the development of contact dermatitis by modulating inflammatory responses, as indicated by its use in conditions that are linked to this outcome. The overlapping pathways highlight a potential mechanism where corticosteroids, through their anti-inflammatory properties, may influence the progression of skin conditions that ultimately lead to contact dermatitis. While the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated, the integration of these pathways underscores the role of corticosteroids in the pathogenesis of contact dermatitis, particularly in inflammatory skin disorders.",
